        "briefDescription": "Under this act, any statewide association that facilitates interscholastic activities for secondary school students shall be overseen by a board of directors appointed by the Governor, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate.   The term of office of each director shall be four years, with the initial appointments staggered such that two members shall serve terms of two years and three members shall serve terms of four years.  If the General Assembly is not in session when a position on ",
