        "billSuffix": 1154,
        "session": "261",
        "chamber": "senate",
        "title": "Establishes the \"Act Against Abusive Website Access Litigation\"",
        "briefDescription": "This act creates the \"Act Against Abusive Website Access Litigation\". The Attorney General, on behalf of a class of residents of this state or any resident of this state who is subject to litigation that alleges any website access violation, may file a civil action against the party, attorney, or law firm that initiated such litigation for a determination as to whether such litigation alleging a website access violation is abusive litigation. A civil action alleging a website access claim is con",
        "lrNumber": "5684S.02I",
        "currentStatus": "referred",
        "currentCommittee": "committee:senate:general_laws",
