        "billSuffix": 1155,
        "session": "261",
        "chamber": "senate",
        "title": "Establishes the \"Missouri Respond, Innovate, Succeed and Empower (RISE) Act\" relating to accommodations for students with disabilities at public institutions of higher education",
        "briefDescription": "This act creates the \"Missouri Respond, Innovate, Succeed, and Empower (RISE) Act\".  Under this act, a public institution of higher education shall adopt a policy that specifies the types of documentation the institution shall accept to determine a student's eligibility for disability accommodations.  The act lists the types of documentation that shall be accepted, including documentation related to Individualized Education Programs (IEPs) and 504 plans developed under federal law, provided that",
        "lrNumber": "3856S.02I",
        "currentStatus": "referred",
        "currentCommittee": "committee:senate:education",
        "effectiveDate": "2026-08-28",
        "introducedDate": null,
