        "title": "Modifies provisions relating to multiple employer self-insured health plans",
        "briefDescription": "Current law defines a multiple employer self-insured health plan as one that is either offered by a staff or employee leasing company or established or maintained for the purpose of offering or providing health, dental, or short-term disability benefits to employees of two or more employers. This act modifies such definition by providing that a multiple employer self-insured health plan also includes one that is established or maintained for the purpose of offering or providing health, dental, o",
        "lrNumber": "5952S.01I",
