        "billPrefix": "SB",
        "billSuffix": 1531,
        "session": "261",
        "chamber": "senate",
        "title": "Creates provisions relating to modifying child custody and visitation orders",
        "briefDescription": "This act permits a party to request the court to issue a temporary custody or visitation order during the pendency of a motion to modify any judgment pertaining to child custody or visitation.  Such orders shall remain in effect until the disposition of the motion to modify or further order of the court.  The order may be granted with notice to opposing parties and after a hearing, although notice may be waived in emergency situations; provided that orders issued where notice is waived shall be ",
