        "billSuffix": 1536,
        "session": "261",
        "chamber": "senate",
        "title": "Establishes the Designated Health Care Decision-Maker Act, which authorizes certain persons to make health care decisions for certain incapacitated persons",
        "briefDescription": "This act establishes the Designated Health Care Decision-Maker Act. Specifically, a health care provider or health care facility may rely on good faith and reasonable medical judgment for health care decisions made by designated health care decision-makers if two physicians determine that an incapacitated patient does not have a guardian with medical decision-making authority, a durable power of attorney for health care, is not a child under juvenile court jurisdiction, nor has any other known p",
